  "note": "On the Boris scheme the argument of the gyration eigenvalue and the phase advance measured on the run agree to 4e-16, which is parker1991's 2 arctan(Omega h / 2) recovered from a numerical Jacobian.  On the learned maps they do not agree at all: the four HNN cells have no complex eigenvalue on the orbit whatsoever -- all four eigenvalues are real, in reciprocal pairs -- and the SympNet's complex pair sits at 0.263 to 0.269 where the run advances by 0.29997 per step.  The Jacobian rotates the tangent space; only for a linear map is that the rotation of the state.  So the argument channel fails to transfer from the linear case for exactly the reason the modulus channel does, and the frequency error quoted here and in Section 7 of the manuscript has to come from the run."
